      "case": "negative count reachable only by direct field mutation",
      "decision": "Index with ((count as i64) as u64) % 8, giving 7 for -1, 6 for -2, etc. — never a negative index.",
      "rationale": "The binary sign-extends with movslq then divides with unsigned `div`, which is precisely C++'s int -> size_t conversion in `count_ % frames_.size()`. Verified: show(-1,8) -> `⣷ ...` (index 7). A Rust port using `rem_euclid` would also give 7 here, but would differ for a hypothetical unsigned-wrap value; the cast chain is the exact transliteration."
